WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.062
AGE and direct subtraction both compare two temporal values, but their emphasis differs.

00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:10.182
AGE expresses a symbolic calendar interval using years, months, and days.

00:00:10.182 --> 00:00:17.297
Direct subtraction gives the elapsed interval between two timestamps.

00:00:17.297 --> 00:00:22.617
For hospital length of stay, direct subtraction is usually easier to interpret.

00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:25.122
For calendar-style age differences, AGE may be more natural.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:30.552
Date arithmetic should reflect the business definition.

00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:36.397
Calendar age, elapsed hours, and number of midnights are not always the same measure.

00:00:36.397 --> 00:00:43.287
In healthcare, length of stay may have an operational definition that differs from simple timestamp

00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:45.360
subtraction. Document the unit and the rule.
